{"origin": "Paris", "destination": "New York", "departure_date": "2026-05-10", "return_date": "2026-05-20", "passengers": 1}
The user expects the system to leverage this `flights_search_input` to suggest a new, exotic destination while retaining the original origin, dates, and passenger count. The final "ConversationalOutput" should contain an "agent_decision" of 'inspiration_agent', with "flights_search_output" updated to include an exotic "destination" (e.g., 'Tokyo', 'Bangkok', or 'Rio de Janeiro') and an engaging "agent_response" pitching this new destination. The original `origin`, `departure_date`, `return_date`, and `passengers` in "flights_search_output" should remain unchanged.
